{#
edit = "removes `pub def extra` from `m0.ray`, between its helpers and `work0`, which `main` in `main.ray` still calls, so the check reports that `extra` is not found"

[[knobs]]
name = "modules"
base = 3
adds = "file modules like `m1.ray`, which `main.ray` declares and calls and the edit does not touch"

[[knobs]]
name = "edited_functions"
base = 3
adds = "functions like `work1` to `m0.ray`, the edited module, below the removed function"
#}
{#
Only `main` calls the removed function, so the work should not grow with the
modules or functions that do not call it, apart from the projections of the
table of `m0.ray`: the table is a firewall, so a changed table reruns the
projection of every symbol of the file.

Known gaps, which the snapshot shows: every `work<j>` has the parameter list
`(seed: int32)` and return type `int32` of `extra`, and a branch of the token
tree whose text another branch has takes its ID from how many come before it,
so adding or removing `extra` renumbers them and recomputes the signature and
the typed AST of every function below it. And `FilePathKey` reads the whole
table index, which a new or removed symbol changes, so it dirties every query
that reads a source file of the target, which all turn out clean.
#}
{% import "shared/program.ray.j2" as program %}
{% set extra %}


pub def extra(seed: int32) -> int32:
    return seed + 1
{% endset %}
--- file main.ray
{{ program.main(modules, calls=["m0.extra(0)"]) }}
{% for m in range(modules) %}
--- file m{{ m }}.ray
{% if m == 0 %}
{{ program.module(m, edited_functions, items="" if edit else extra) }}
{% else %}
{{ program.module(m, 3) }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
